 "youtube": {
  "title": "Ada Blackjack: How Did She Survive Alone on Wrangel Island?",
  "description": "Ada Blackjack was the only one who came back from Wrangel Island. In 1921 four young explorers took her, their Iñupiat seamstress, to a frozen island north of Siberia.\n\nThe food ran out. In January 1923 three men set off across the sea ice for help and were never seen again. Ada nursed the last man, Lorne Knight, until he died of scurvy. Alone and terrified of polar bears, she taught herself to shoot, trapped foxes and built a lookout platform, until the schooner Donaldson arrived in August 1923. An Arctic survival story with one survivor and a cat named Vic.\n\nSubscribe to Stickstory for one true survival story a day. Could you have lasted alone on that island? Tell me in the comments!\n\n#shorts #adablackjack #survivalstory #stickstory",
